---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Set Easy - Support"
  description="Help with Set Easy, the strength training log for iPhone and Apple Watch."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/set-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>
        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Set Easy?</p>
          <p>Email <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Set%20Easy%20Support" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How does Set Easy pick today's workout?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Your workouts take turns: the one you did longest ago is up next. Tap Swap on Today to pick another one for the day, or start an empty workout and add exercises as you go.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I log a set?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Start a workout and each exercise lists its sets with last time's weight and your target reps. Change them if you need to, then tap the circle to check the set off. The rest timer starts on its own; Skip ends it early.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What counts as a personal best?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">A working set heavier than any you've done for that exercise in an earlier workout. The first time you do an exercise sets the bar. Warm-up sets don't count.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I use Set Easy on Apple Watch?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Install it from the Watch app on your iPhone. Your workouts appear on the watch with last time's weights; turn the Digital Crown to set weight and reps and tap Done after each set. Finished workouts go to History on your iPhone the next time Set Easy is open nearby.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I connect Apple Health?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Open the menu, then Settings, Connections, Apple Health, and tap Continue. Set Easy saves the workouts you finish and reads heart rate during them. To change access later, open the Health app and go to Sharing, Apps, Set Easy.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I bring my history from another app?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Yes. Export a CSV file from Strong or Hevy, then in Set Easy open Settings, Data, Import history. Workouts already in Set Easy are skipped.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I back up my data?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">In Settings, Data, tap Back up and save the file to Files or another device. Restore a backup adds anything that's missing and never deletes.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does it work without an account?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">Yes. Set Easy has no accounts and works offline. Your data stays on your devices.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
